Windows: Let the statistics' shared memory grow on macOS.

With FEX_PROFILESTATS=1 FEX keeps a slot of counters for each thread in the
shared memory object fex-<pid>-stats. It starts with one page, 38 slots, and
is made larger with ftruncate when they are used up. macOS lets the size of a
shared memory object be set once only, so the second ftruncate fails there.
The failed call reported a size of 0, which was taken for the new size: the
next thread got no slot, and AllocateSlot wrote to a null pointer. Call of
Duty: WWII died of that at its start (access violation in
FEX::SHMStats::StatAllocBase::AllocateSlot), as does any program with more
than 38 threads.

On macOS the object now gets its full size, 4 MB, when it is made; its pages
cost nothing until they are written, and growing only maps more of it. A
failed call to grow leaves the size as it was, on every system, so that the
thread goes without counters instead.

LOCAL TO THIS PORT, NOT FOR FEX. Applied by macos/build-fex.sh to
github.com/athei/FEX at 8425ea974e072821c75969723efe49cca605200c. Written
with an AI assistant (Claude). FEX takes no AI-generated code contributions
(its CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md and CONTRIBUTING.md), so this patch must not be
sent to it as a pull request. What was found may be reported to its
developers, for them to write their own change.
